<section id="how" class="how">
  <div class="container inner">
    <div class="intro">
      <h2>Set up in three steps without touching the server.</h2>
      <p>
        If <code>ssh mini</code> works without a prompt, Nearhost works. It reuses your SSH config,
        including ProxyJump, agents and keychain identities, and writes nothing to the remote
        machine.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="steps">
      <div class="card">
        <div class="num">01</div>
        <h3>Add a server</h3>
        <p>
          Pick a host alias from <code>~/.ssh/config</code> or type <code>user@host</code>. Nearhost
          checks that it connects without a prompt and shows OpenSSH's own output if it doesn't.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="num">02</div>
        <h3>Add a project</h3>
        <p>
          Point at a path. Nearhost reads its <code>.env</code> over SFTP, and with the official
          presets its Compose and Vite config, and proposes the ports: which one is the web app,
          which need a loopback forward, which to ignore.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <div class="num">03</div>
        <h3>Open it</h3>
        <p>
          It starts as soon as you add it: Nearhost adds a hosts entry, issues a certificate from
          its local CA and routes <code>https://myapp.test</code> through the SSH tunnel. WebSockets
          and hot reload pass through the same tunnel. Press <code>o</code> to open it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .how {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--nh-line);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--nh-ground) 92%, var(--nh-surface));
  }
  .inner {
    padding-block: 96px 56px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 56px;
  }
  .intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--nh-font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: var(--nh-track-display);
  }
  .intro p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--nh-body);
    font-size: 18px;
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--nh-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
  }
  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 28px;
    background: var(--nh-ground);
    border: 1px solid var(--nh-line);
    border-radius: 12px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .num {
    font-family: var(--nh-font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--nh-faint);
  }
  h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--nh-font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 24px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .card p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--nh-muted);
    font-size: 16px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 719px) {
    .steps {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
